From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mesh-LLM CI <ci@mesh-llm.local>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 02:04:42 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] skippy: add receipt recorder and replay

skippy_model_set_receipt_recorder reports, after each computed ubatch,
the residual stream entering every stage layer, the stage output, and
each layer's attn_q, attn_k and attn_v outputs and attention output,
with the ubatch geometry replay needs: tokens, sequences, positions,
output rows, KV cells, n_kv and the stage input rows. It also reports
KV-cache changes, so the caller can refuse sequences a replay cannot
reproduce. The receipt tensors are flagged as graph outputs in the
build and reserve graphs, so the planned allocation keeps them, and
are copied into one of two pinned host blocks, used in turn, so a
caller can hash a ubatch while the next one computes.

skippy_model_replay_receipt replays recorded steps in a scratch
context created with the stage context's parameters, forcing the
recorded KV cells and n_kv, and also reports the matmul inputs and
outputs of one challenged layer. Verifiable inference receipts commit
to the residual stream and open a challenged layer by replay instead
of storing every matmul column. Replaces skippy_model_set_receipt_tap
and the eval-callback hooks it needed. ABI 0.1.74 -> 0.1.75.
